From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mvx_log: walk dentry children as an hlist on 6.8+

Building against 7.2 fails with:

  mvx_log.c:153:39: error: 'struct dentry' has no member named 'd_subdirs'
  mvx_log.c:153:52: error: 'struct dentry' has no member named 'd_child';
  did you mean 'd_children'?

6.8 converted the dentry child list from a list_head to an hlist, renaming
d_subdirs to d_children and d_child to d_sib. Add a version-gated branch
using hlist_for_each_entry() and leave the existing branches in place so the
driver still builds against older trees.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor tree]
The CIX P1 VPU driver is a vendor drop with no upstream submission path;
carried downstream only.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
--- a/driver/mvx_log.c
+++ b/driver/mvx_log.c
@@ -149,7 +149,9 @@
     struct dentry *child;
 
     /* Loop over directory entries in mvx/drain/. */
-#if (KERNEL_VERSION(3, 18, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
+#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 8, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
+    hlist_for_each_entry(child, &parent->d_children, d_sib)
+#elif (KERNEL_VERSION(3, 18, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
     list_for_each_entry(child, &parent->d_subdirs, d_child)
 #else
     list_for_each_entry(child, &parent->d_subdirs, d_u.d_child)
